<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arinna</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arinna was a Hittite holy city in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, a short distance from the capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hattusa">Hattusa</a>, whose exact site has not been identified. It was the cult centre of the sun goddess of Arinna, the chief goddess of the Hittite state and patron of its kings, a deity inherited from the earlier <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hattians">Hattians</a>. Hittite queens served as her high priestesses.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arinna.jpg" alt="Arinna" width="320" height="217" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bernard Gagnon · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Orthostates,_Alaca_H%C3%B6y%C3%BCk_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
